<title>UK: Lex Service awarded British army contract.</title>
<headline>Lex Service awarded British army contract.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>British auto retail and service company Lex Services Plc said on Thursday it was part of a consortium that received a British army contract worth over 150 million stg for the next seven years.</p>
<p>Lex said its portion of the contract, to provide support services for the Aldershot Garrison, amounted to 28 million stg. Other members of the consortium included Lex Transfleet, Primary Management, and W.S. Atkins.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
